<title>USA: Part of Mobil coker remains shut after fire.</title>
<headline>Part of Mobil coker remains shut after fire.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mobil Corp said part of the coker unit at its 130,000 barrel-per-day refinery in Torrance, Calif., remained shut late Thursday due to a fire which blazed in the unit from around 1430 PST to 1525 PST.</p>
<p>A company spokeswoman said investigators were not able to assess the damage to the unit or say how the fire would affect supplies of refined products.</p>
<p>The cause of the fire remains under investigation, she said.</p>
<p>The refinery makes about 105,000 bpd of gasoline.</p>
<p>-- David Brinkerhoff, Los Angeles bureau +1 213 380 2014</p>
</text>
